  "change": {
    "behavior": "Ordinary computed assignment references retain their evaluated raw key register through GetIndex and SetIndex instead of emitting an eager ToPropertyKey instruction. The shared index access path accepts tagged nonnegative integers and canonical decimal-index strings; already-string and symbol keys do not undergo a redundant ToPropertyKey call on the slow path.",
    "representation": "The key remains the existing VM Value in the existing register. Canonical array-index parsing remains owned by object_static::array_index; no second key table, opcode, or serialized format was added.",
    "ordering": "The base and key expressions are evaluated once. GetIndex performs key coercion before the getter and right-hand side; SetIndex performs key coercion at the write boundary. This matches local Node 26.10.0 for object keys whose ToPrimitive is observable.",
    "scope": "This candidate intentionally follows the configured Node compatibility oracle on compound computed assignment. Node/V8 invokes observable ToPropertyKey twice for the affected object-key cases; the current Test262 cases require one conversion."
  },
